/*
  protocol/crypto.spthy -- CRYPTO LAYER for the secure_email ceremony (C1).
  Declares the message-encryption primitives this ceremony needs. Kept OUT of core/types.spthy
  on purpose: the human layer (masks/stressors/transitions) is ceremony-agnostic and must not
  drag in email crypto. builtins are theory-level declarations; #include-ing this fragment inside
  a theory begin..end pulls them in (nested includes work -- see repo MEMORY.md lesson 4).

    asymmetric-encryption : pk/1, aenc/2, adec/2   -- Method 2 (OpenPGP, end-to-end)
    symmetric-encryption  : senc/2, sdec/2         -- Method 3 (password-based)

  The two methods map onto Proton Mail (proton.me/support/how-to-use-pgp, /password-protected-emails):
    PGP : aenc(m, pk(skB)) -- only the recipient's private key skB decrypts.
    PW  : senc(m, pw)      -- the passphrase pw is the secret; it must travel out-of-band.
*/

builtins: asymmetric-encryption, symmetric-encryption
